  "prediction": "**Summary of the Department of Defense's Foreign Currency Budget Rates**\n\nThe Department of Defense (DOD) establishes foreign currency budget rates to determine its funding needs for overseas expenditures. These rates are used to calculate gains or losses due to foreign currency fluctuations. The report examines DOD's revised foreign currency budget rates since 2009 and their relationship to DOD's projected Operation and Maintenance (O&M) and Military Personnel (MILPERS) funding needs.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n1. DOD revised its foreign currency budget rates in fiscal years 2014-2016 to more closely align with market rates, resulting in decreased projected O&M and MILPERS funding needs.\n2. The revised budget rates also decreased potential gains and losses in the amount of funds available for planned overseas expenditures.\n3. DOD's use of revised foreign currency budget rates resulted in a decrease of $2.7 billion in projected funding needs from fiscal years 2009-2017.\n4. The Army's Foreign Currency Fluctuations Defense (O&M) reports are inaccurate and cannot be used to reliably track gains or losses due to foreign currency fluctuations.\n5. DOD lacks complete and accurate data to effectively manage foreign currency gains and losses, hindering sound decision-making and resource stewardship.\n\n**Recommendations:**\n\n1. The Under Secretary of Defense (Comptroller) should conduct a review of foreign currency rates used at disbursement to determine cost-saving opportunities.\n2. The Under Secretary of Defense (Comptroller) should analyze realized and projected losses to determine the necessary size of the Foreign Currency Fluctuations Defense (FCFD) account balance.\n3. The Under Secretary of Defense (Comptroller) should revise the Financial Management Regulation to include guidance on ensuring complete and accurate data in Foreign Currency Fluctuations Defense (O&M) reports.\n4. The Secretary of the Army should develop a plan with timelines for implementing changes to its General Fund Enterprise Business System to accurately record disbursements.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nDOD's revised foreign currency budget rates have resulted in decreased projected funding needs and potential gains and losses. However, DOD still lacks complete and accurate data to effectively manage foreign currency gains and losses. Implementing the recommended changes will help DOD improve its management of foreign currency fluctuations and ensure sound decision-making and resource stewardship.",
